<title>POLAND: Polish household heating prices to rise Oct 1.</title>
<headline>Polish household heating prices to rise Oct 1.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish household heating and hot water prices will increase by about five percent from October 1, a finance ministry official said.</p>
<p>Marek Borkowski told Reuters the increase, the third this year, would bring the total rise in heating and hot water prices to 19.1 percent, as envisaged in this year's budget.</p>
<p>The ministry said in a statement the rises were necessary to make up for rising costs, especially coal.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
